KG42.register("rules-9f2de98b5acdeb7046bf4951",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R017","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R017","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","name":"Demand submission","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The BS mechanism requires energy bids using the specification in Formula (A18), including its requested-energy quantities, as used in SDR. Scope: Requested-energy quantities within BS energy bids.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function bidding.demand under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Requested-energy quantities within BS energy bids.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R017-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The BS mechanism requires energy bids using the specification in Formula (A18), including its requested-energy quantities, as used in SDR. Scope: Requested-energy quantities within BS energy bids.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-08","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p27-c2r2__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":27,"printed_page":"1019","section":"A.2.3","anchor_text":"(A27) r agent under mid-market rate mechanism. energy cost and income evenly throughout the time hor","equation_id":"A28","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-27.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Bill sharing is a mechanism in which all the prosumers share the energy cost and income evenly throughout the time horizon. The energy bids required by the BS mechanism are the same as those in the SDR mechanism as described by Formula (A18). The internal price is calculated by\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = r_t^{retail} \\cdot \\frac{\\sum_{t \\in T_u^+} \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} \\sum_{t \\in T_l^+} e_{n,t}^{bid}}, & T_u^+ = \\{ t \\mid \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid} > 0, t \\in T \\}, T_l^+ = \\{ t \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} > 0, t \\in T \\} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = r_t^{export} \\cdot \\frac{\\sum_{t \\in T_u^-} \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{n,t}^{bid}|}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} \\sum_{t \\in T_l^-} |e_{n,t}^{bid}|}, & T_u^- = \\{ t \\mid \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, t \\in T \\}, T_l^- = \\{ t \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, t \\in T \\} \\end{cases}  (A28)\n\nFormula (A28) actually distributes the total energy cost and income of the whole energy sharing region among the prosumers according the amount of energy they consume and generate. Taking the buying price part as an example, r_t^{retail} \\cdot \\sum_{t \\in T_u^+} \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid} is the total energy cost of the whole region for importing electricity from the retailer throughout the time horizon, which is divided by \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} \\sum_{t \\in T_l^+} e_{n,t}^{bid}, the sum of each individual prosumer's total positive net energy consumption throughout the time horizon."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No typed demand-bid variable, such as the requested-energy quantity e_{n,t}^{bid}, is declared in this frozen rule. The referenced Formula (A18) is not present in the supplied evidence and C.1 supplied no x objects for this graph draft; this does not assert that the source lacks variables.","empty_theta_reason":"No typed parameters are declared in this frozen rule. C.1 supplied no theta objects for this graph draft. Parameters that appear in the BS price formula (A28) are associated with pricing.local in other rules, not with the bidding.demand node under this rule's evidence."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-pricing","v141-a-M03-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"bidding.demand","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-08","quote":"The energy bids required by the BS mechanism are the same as those in the SDR mechanism as described by Formula (A18)."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"e81c2cc85e4c31603c354198ec3c2e85b515c1d2d00073dc822e807e9aa99cdb","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The frozen rule contains only the node bidding.demand and no edges. The supporting evidence v141-b-g07-ev-08 states that BS energy bids must be the same as SDR energy bids described by Formula (A18), but the supplied evidence does not transcribe Formula (A18) and does not provide the bid-quantity definitions needed to formalize requested-energy quantities. The existing procedural constraint is therefore preserved as not_formalized; formalization requires a verified extraction of Formula (A18) and C.1 objects for the bid quantities.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R017-C001","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The constraint is a demand-submission requirement attaching to the frozen bidding.demand node. No edge is present in this rule to link bidding.demand to another node."}],"revision_requests":["B: re-extract and supply Formula (A18) from Appendix A.2.1 (page 26, SDR energy-bid specification) as a verified evidence item for mechanism v141-a-M03 / rule v141-c-R017, because v141-b-g07-ev-08 only states that BS uses the SDR bid specification described by Formula (A18) and does not include Formula (A18) itself.","C.1: add a variable object for the requested-energy quantity e_{n,t}^{bid} under node bidding.demand, with indices n ∈ PA and t ∈ T and unit/domain only where supported by the verified source extraction of Formula (A18).","C.1: if Formula (A18) is verified, add any needed supporting parameters and indices (e.g. prosumer and time indices and PV/appliance terms appearing in A18) to the bidding.demand side of this rule, without moving them from their proper pricing or decision-model nodes.","C.1: consider whether any edge from bidding.demand to pricing.local is needed for the BS bid quantities only if supported by a verified extraction of the BS price formula, since R017 currently has no E entries."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
